{"availability":"available","full":"pocket-nexus/quickjs-oxide","name":"quickjs-oxide","description":"An independent Rust rewrite of QuickJS targeting semantic feature parity","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":66,"forks":2,"created":"2026-07-10T18:47:53Z","updated":"2026-10-17T10:57:36Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pocket-nexus.github.io/quickjs-oxide/","topics":["javascript-engine","quickjs","rust"],"demo":"https://pocket-nexus.github.io/quickjs-oxide/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T12:30:42.146Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T12:30:42.146Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T12:30:42.146Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:01:04.187Z","stars":63,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-13T04:14:56.264Z","stars":65,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-17T12:30:42.146Z","stars":66,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A JavaScript engine written entirely in safe Rust, with zero unsafe, that reproduces the behavior of QuickJS 2026-06-04.","Within the Test262 scope that QuickJS 2026-06-04 runs, quickjs-oxide passes 83,304 of 83,562 variants (99.691%). QuickJS's test262.conf skips the other 18,475 of the 102,037 variants; across the full corpus the pass rate is 81.641%.","unsafecode = \"forbid\", so the compiler rejects unsafe anywhere in the engine, the CLI and the WebAssembly bindings. The garbage collector, compiler, VM, regular expression engine and Unicode tables are all safe Rust; the only third-party code in the engine is num-bigint and num-traits for BigInt arithmetic."],"features":["Zero unsafe. Every crate in the workspace sets","Fast without unsafe. On the Octane suite it outperforms most Rust","Same behavior as QuickJS. Every failing Test262 variant is one QuickJS","Runs where you need it. A qjs command line, a Rust embedding API and a"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pocket-nexus/quickjs-oxide/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"16c5633ce722d69917db362251a58cdfb